WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.304
In the time of Emperor Shenzong of Song, the emperor appointed Wang Anshi to carry out a series of reforms.

00:00:05.654 --> 00:00:10.382
The young emperor hoped the country would grow strong and the people prosperous.

00:00:10.732 --> 00:00:15.676
The reforms aimed to improve the state's finances, military, and social problems.

00:00:16.026 --> 00:00:21.450
But the reforms sparked fierce debate; some supported them, others opposed them.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:26.408
At court, the ministers often argued until their faces were red.

00:00:26.758 --> 00:00:31.798
Sima Guang and other conservative ministers firmly opposed the new laws.

00:00:32.148 --> 00:00:37.884
They worried the new laws were being pushed too fast and would trouble the people.

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:42.146
Wang Anshi was dismissed twice, and in the end the reforms did not succeed.

00:00:42.496 --> 00:00:47.488
After leaving the court, he returned to his hometown and lived quietly.

00:00:47.838 --> 00:00:53.094
The Wang Anshi Reforms became one of the most important events in the political history of the Northern Song.

00:00:53.444 --> 00:00:58.004
When later generations talk about the Northern Song, they always mention this great reform.

